# The build host's toolchains (docs/CR-PLAN.md section 1, track CT1),
# fetched by tools/cr/toolchain.sh into ~/.cache/jamos/ on the build host
# (the PC's WSL), each pinned by size and SHA-256. One line each:
#
#   <name> <version> <size in bytes> <sha256> <url> [<file name>]
#
# (the file name, when the URL's last part is no name: a cloud object's hash)
#
# clang: Chromium's own prebuilt clang and lld for Linux x86_64, the
# compiler Chromium 155.0.8059.39 is tested with: the package its
# tools/clang/scripts/update.py fetches (CLANG_REVISION
# llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b, CLANG_SUB_REVISION 27, RELEASE_VERSION
# 24). Moves with Chromium's version (CR-PLAN section 14): read the new
# version's update.py, fetch, hash, change this line.
clang llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-27 57243988 83f4a4ea3292bfc236d85575fa7af27d39180d88534bc3117b73ad1df34bb959 https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/chromium-browser-clang/Linux_x64/clang-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-27.tar.xz
# cmake: for ports/llvm-runtimes (LLVM's runtimes want 3.20 or newer;
# Ubuntu 24.04's apt has 3.28 but nothing is installed system-wide for
# Jam OS), Kitware's wheel from PyPI installed into the ports builder's
# venv, ~/.cache/jamos/tools (docs/TESTING.md), beside Meson and Ninja.
cmake 3.31.10 27808794 2f766bb46367e5e0559fa33184653754bce044583a06014dcaebf8e6dff8a1f1 https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/f4/2e/cefc60143950ca1a8dda26d4c8484e6fc406db16e7ca098ebae549de35f9/cmake-3.31.10-py3-none-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
# rust: Chromium's own prebuilt Rust for Linux x86_64 (rustc 1.100.0-dev
# with cargo, rust-src and its vendored crates, bindgen), the package its
# tools/rust/update_rust.py fetches (RUST_REVISION
# 1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0, RUST_SUB_REVISION 1, named with
# the clang revision above, without clang's sub-revision). The target's
# standard library is built from its rust-src (ports/cr-rust-hello), as
# Chromium's GN does: no std for Jam OS is fetched. Moves with Chromium's
# version, together with the clang line.
rust 1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b 276475500 793d75e2aade21579a3bf3be0df82fa569d66b5a4ad8c2e8eef64310e6e8202c https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/chromium-browser-clang/Linux_x64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz
# gperf: Chromium's build runs it (Blink's and net's perfect hashes) and
# nothing on the build host is to be depended on: built from this source
# into ~/.cache/jamos/tools (docs/TESTING.md), where the ports builder, the
# PC check and later Chromium builds find it first on PATH. 3.1 is what
# Debian and Ubuntu ship.
gperf 3.1 1215925 588546b945bba4b70b6a3a616e80b4ab466e3f33024a352fc2198112cdbb3ae2 https://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/gperf/gperf-3.1.tar.gz
# node: Chromium's own Node.js for the build host (v24.12.0, its
# third_party/node/update_node_binaries), the object its DEPS pins for
# src/third_party/node/linux (bucket chromium-nodejs, object_name, sha256sum,
# size_bytes). The source tarball doesn't bring it (DEPS fetches it from
# Google Cloud Storage); Chromium's build runs it (WebUI's TypeScript, the
# resources' bundling). Unpacked into ~/.cache/jamos/toolchains/node-<version>/
# (node-linux-x64/bin/node), where ports/chromium's build links it into the
# tree. The sixth word is the file's name in the cache (the URL's last part
# is the object's hash). Moves with Chromium's version (its DEPS).
node v24.12.0 53566970 bdea62a6857735d62165ec97242d79a693564c72d551890c4d009d2355abf14c https://storage.googleapis.com/chromium-nodejs/744e6926ffdd4a4fb2080ae2b9ce4575490261e7 node-linux-x64-v24.12.0.tar.gz
# sysroot: Chromium's own Debian bullseye amd64 sysroot (glibc's headers and
# libraries), its build/linux/sysroot_scripts/sysroots.json's bullseye_amd64
# (the object named by its SHA-256). Chromium's host tools (protoc, V8's
# mksnapshot and torque, the generators) are built against it by the host
# toolchain (use_sysroot=true), so they run on the build host whatever its
# distribution has installed, while the target is built against Jam OS's.
# Unpacked into ~/.cache/jamos/toolchains/sysroot-<version>/.
sysroot bullseye_amd64-20250129T203412Z-2 19727236 52d61d4446ffebfaa3dda2cd02da4ab4876ff237853f46d273e7f9b666652e1d https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/chrome-linux-sysroot/52d61d4446ffebfaa3dda2cd02da4ab4876ff237853f46d273e7f9b666652e1d debian_bullseye_amd64_sysroot-20250129T203412Z-2.tar.xz
# test-fonts: Chromium's test fonts, the object its DEPS pins for
# src/third_party/test_fonts/test_fonts (bucket chromium-fonts): the tarball
# leaves them out, and base_unittests' and the other tests' data need them.
# Unpacked into ~/.cache/jamos/toolchains/test-fonts-<version>/, which
# ports/chromium's build links into the tree. Moves with Chromium's DEPS.
test-fonts 9c07d19d9c5e 33413117 f0e9628f9e43e3f3476cde06a1849058de460e0e037b7449ce0d42b9a73c37d5 https://storage.googleapis.com/chromium-fonts/9c07d19d9c5ee1ff94f717e6fb17e0c8c354e6f9 test_fonts-9c07d19d9c5e.tar.gz
# go: the Go toolchain Dawn's DEPS pins (dawn_go_version 1.26.6, CIPD's
# infra/3pp/tools/go), here Go's own release of that version, by its published
# SHA-256: Dawn's build runs `go run` of its source generator (Tint's
# sources, offline: GOPROXY=off). Unpacked into
# ~/.cache/jamos/toolchains/go-<version>/ (go/bin/go), which
# ports/chromium's build links into the tree. Moves with Dawn's DEPS.
go 1.26.6 66890545 708effb774be8237570d0add163225abbdfaf4fca28b2611df167beba4feef89 https://go.dev/dl/go1.26.6.linux-amd64.tar.gz
